@startuml
title Default Synchronisation Order (Remote-First)

start
:Validate authentication, service reachability\nand system time safety gates;
note right
  Operating context:
  normal ~--sync or ~--monitor reconciliation
  without ~--local-first.

  "Remote-first" describes ordering only.
  It does not mean online content may blindly
  overwrite unique local data.
end note

:Enumerate Microsoft OneDrive online state;
note right
  Online state may come from Graph /delta
  or a generated hierarchy walk depending
  on scope and operating mode.
end note
:Filter, classify and apply required online changes locally;
note right
  If an online file must replace an existing local file,
  the transactional download path re-checks the local
  canonical file before commit. Unique local content is
  preserved with safeBackup before replacement.
end note

:Process known database state against\nthe local filesystem;
note right
  Detect locally modified or deleted objects that were
  previously tracked. The database provides the last
  successfully applied reconciliation baseline.
end note

if (~--download-only?) then (yes)
  :Skip upload-side local filesystem scan;
else (no)
  :Scan local filesystem for new data;
  :Upload eligible new local files / directories;
  note right
    A safeBackup created earlier in the cycle is itself
    local data. It may be discovered and uploaded as a
    new file unless excluded through skip_file.
  end note

  if (force_children_scan enabled?) then (yes)
    :Skip duplicate final /children traversal;
  else (no)
    :Perform final online true-up;
  endif
endif

stop
@enduml
